    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d99">

                <pb facs="0129" n="79" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg79"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.51/378</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Archangel</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-10-24T15:00:00+03:31"><hi rendition="#italic">October 24,
                                1918, 3 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received October 24, 12.54
                        p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>513. Referring to my 401, September 14, 4 p.m., and 423 September 24, 7
                        p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d99-f1"/> British financial expert arrived here
                    with one hundred million new rubles which proposes paying British soldiers and
                    for other necessary expenses. The government is in financial straits but I have
                    objected to their accepting such new rubles, if tendered, as I think it [they]
                    will be. What understanding, if any, have we on the subject? Have you any
                    instructions?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
